                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9c03ab3-a266-37f7-b958-65722668556c",
                        "entry_id": "08edba4e-7adb-3017-9d4e-8deb620c6d6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of the Channel Islands; notable inter alia for its local government containing one of the last vestiges of feudalism in Europe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8486dddb-32f7-33ef-821f-e1ff4c336456",
                        "entry_id": "08edba4e-7adb-3017-9d4e-8deb620c6d6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A minor river in Dumfries and Galloway council area and Cumbria, forming part of the border between Scotland and England, which flows into the tidal Esk at Gretna; in full, the River Sark."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "453395cb-c711-405d-a4b4-f91bb9061a35",
                                "sense_id": "8486dddb-32f7-33ef-821f-e1ff4c336456",
                                "text": "I have often been amused by travellers pointing out, first the Eden, just north of the station, and then the Esk, which young Lochinvar swam, as the Border; the real boundary is, of course, the little river Sark, just south of the Caledonian station at Gretna; […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
